lish the beginning of this scene.\n\nMaintain the same burning village setting\nand natural visual continuity.\n\nKeep the scene focused only on Riven and her father.\n\n\n=== TECHNICAL ===\n\n16:9 cinematic live-action dark fantasy.\n\nBurning village at dusk.\n\nGrounded realistic human movement.\n\nNatural English dialogue and lip sync.\n\nSlow, restrained cinematic camera movement.\n\nWarm firelight through smoke and drifting ash.\n\nIntimate and emotionally restrained.\n\nKeep the scene simple.\n\nNo combat.\n\nNo subtitles.\n\nNo background music.\n\n\n=== SCENE ===\n\nBegin directly with Riven kneeling beside her father.\n\nHer father remains weakly resting\nagainst the collapsed wooden debris.\n\nHis hand is already touching Riven's face.\n\nRiven stays very close to him.\n\n\nHold this quiet moment.\n\nFather looks into Riven's eyes.\n\nVery weakly, he says:\n\n\"You came back.\"\n\n\nRiven struggles to control her emotions.\n\nShe answers quietly:\n\n\"I came too late.\"\n\n\nFather continues looking at her.\n\nHe is extremely weak,\nbut calm.\n\n\nAfter a brief silence, he asks:\n\n\"Do you remember what I told you?\"\n\n\nRiven understands immediately.\n\nWith tears in her eyes, she answers:\n\n\"Protect those who can't protect themselves.\"\n\n\nFather gives her a small, tired smile.\n\n\nHe quietly says:\n\n\"Then keep going.\"\n\n\nHold on Riven's reaction.\n\nShe wants to respond,\nbut cannot find the words.\n\n\nFather's strength begins to fade.\n\n\nThe hand touching Riven's face\nslowly loses its strength\nand slips downward.\n\n\nRiven quickly catches his hand.\n\n\nShe looks at him and says:\n\n\"Father?\"\n\n\nNo response.\n\n\nRiven waits for him to breathe again.\n\n\nNothing.\n\n\nVery softly, she says:\n\n\"Father...\"\n\n\nRiven realizes he is gone.\n\n\nShe remains beside him,\nstill holding his hand.\n\n\nDo not make Riven scream.\n\nHer grief is quiet and overwhelming.\n\n\nShe slowly lowers her head\nand stays beside her father.\n\n\nT